      "created_at": "2018-04-10T13:07:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-10T13:07:34Z",
      "body": "Hi @Mishef,\r\n\r\nWe send the timestamp, email address and IP address of the user to MailChimp whenever the form is submitted where they store this and belief this should provide a large enough legal basis, but I am not a lawyer so I might be wrong.\r\n\r\nIf we were to implement a \"save consent\" feature in the plugin, what would it ideally look like to you? \r\n\r\nA checkbox that has to be ticket and then stores a number of fields in the database? What fields? Should it include the terms that were agreed to and if so, in what format?\r\n\r\nThanks for thinking along here!",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
